course: dictionary
lesson: 895
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Bise is one of them. You find the right meaning by reading the words around it, which are its context. «The bise blew cold and dry over the snowy valley.» Cold, dry and snowy tell you bise is a wind.
explain: The same word can be used for a greeting. «La bise is a light greeting with cheeks touching and a kiss in the air.» Cheeks and kiss tell you bise here means a light kiss on the cheek, not weather.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. If «a cold wind» makes no sense in the greeting sentence, you have picked the wrong meaning. Then try the other one.
fact: Bise has two meanings: a cold, dry wind, and a light kiss on the cheek used as a greeting.
fact: The wind is a local wind, from the north or north-east over Switzerland and parts of France.
fact: «Faire la bise» means to greet someone with a cheek kiss, in French.
fact: «Grosses bises» means "big kisses" and is often written at the end of a letter.
fact: Bise sounds like "beez". It is not an everyday English word, so context is your best clue.
exercise: «The bise blew cold and dry across the valley all afternoon.» What is a bise here? | *A cold, dry wind | A warm summer rain | A kind of bread | A light kiss on the cheek
exercise: In Paris, Maya meets her aunt and does «faire la bise». What does she do? | Waves from across the street | *Gives a light kiss on each cheek | Shakes hands firmly | Runs out of the room
exercise: Which phrase means "big kisses" and is often written at the end of a letter? | la bise froide | faire la bise | *grosses bises | une bise de vent
test: «La bise is a light greeting with cheeks touching and a kiss in the air.» What does bise mean here? | A cold wind | *A light kiss on the cheek | A mountain path | A letter
test: «The bise howled round the chalet, so we pulled on our coats.» Which meaning fits? | *A cold, dry wind | A greeting in Paris | A type of cake | A light kiss on the cheek
exam: «She gave her grandmother a bise before school.» Which meaning of bise fits best? | *A light kiss on the cheek | A mountain path | A warm drink | A cold wind
